From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: add Baldur DSC 1.2 video support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Baldur (Lenovo Y700 Gen5 / TB323FU) drives a CSOT NT36523 panel in
video mode with DSC 1.2 at 10 bpc over two bonded DSI links.  The
existing Elden paths in 0142 cover the same class of panel; extend
that gated programming to Baldur without changing any other machine.

- dsi_host: select the DSC 1.2 4:4:4 RC table and the existing
  first-line bpg offset for Baldur video mode (no native 4:2:0/4:2:2).
- dpu_encoder: add the downstream DCE initial-line calculation, using
  the active soft-slice count and bits_per_pixel >> 4.
- dpu_encoder_phys_vid: round the compressed timing width up, matching
  the DSI host (952 * 8 / 30 = 254, not the old floor of 253).
- dpu_hw_dsc_1_2: enable FULL_ICH_PREC for Baldur as well as Elden.
- dpu_13_0_kaanapali: advertise FULL_ICH_PREC on every DSC block.

Every new branch is gated on of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur")
plus DSC 1.2 / bpc > 8 where the corresponding Elden path uses those
conditions.  The Elden predicates and both existing helpers are kept
byte-for-byte.

The DSI RC/first-line handling, the extended initial-line algorithm and
the 10-bpc video line rounding are derived from the GPL-2.0-only
tb323fu-linux tree at commit
11a25bf89b65fff48112a91a0b25bc247e7736d8 (patches 0007, 0008 and 0023).
The Baldur-specific changes are original Armada work; no third-party
sign-off is implied.

---
 5 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)
---

